  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Alma",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 56,
    "summary": "Helaman sends an epistle to Moroni, recounting the state of the war with the Lamanites—Antipus and Helaman gain a great victory over the Lamanites—Helaman’s two thousand stripling sons fight with miraculous power, and none of them are slain. Verse 1, about 62 B.C.; verses 2–19, about 66 B.C.; and verses 20–57, about 65–64 B.C.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And now it came to pass in the commencement of the thirtieth year of the reign of the judges, on the second day in the first month, Moroni received an epistle from Helaman, stating the affairs of the people in that quarter of the land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 138,
            "text": "Alma 58:35."
          },
          {
            "start": 151,
            "end": 158,
            "text": "Alma 59:1."
          },
          {
            "start": 210,
            "end": 214,
            "text": "Alma 53:22 (8, 22)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 58:35.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 58:35",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 58,
                    "end": 58,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 35,
                        "end": 35
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "Alma 59:1.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 59:1",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 59,
                    "end": 59,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 1,
                        "end": 1
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:1",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And these are the words which he wrote, saying: My dearly beloved brother, Moroni, as well in the Lord as in the tribulations of our warfare; behold, my beloved brother, I have somewhat to tell you concerning our warfare in this part of the land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:2",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, two thousand of the sons of those men whom Ammon brought down out of the land of Nephi—now ye have known that these were descendants of Laman, who was the eldest son of our father Lehi;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "Alma 53:22."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 53:22.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 53:22",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 53,
                    "end": 53,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 22,
                        "end": 22
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:3",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "Now I need not rehearse unto you concerning their traditions or their unbelief, for thou knowest concerning all these things—",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:4",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore it sufficeth me that I tell you that two thousand of these young men have taken their weapons of war, and would that I should be their leader; and we have come forth to defend our country.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:5",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And now ye also know concerning the covenant which their fathers made, that they would not take up their weapons of war against their brethren to shed blood.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "TG Covenants."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Covenants.",
            "prettyString": "TG Covenants",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Covenants",
                "entryId": "tg-covenants",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:6",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "But in the twenty and sixth year, when they saw our afflictions and our tribulations for them, they were about to break the covenant which they had made and take up their weapons of war in our defence.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 114,
            "end": 119,
            "text": "Alma 24:18 (17–19); 53:13 (13–15)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:7",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "But I would not suffer them that they should break this covenant which they had made, supposing that God would strengthen us, insomuch that we should not suffer more because of the fulfilling the oath which they had taken.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Honesty."
          },
          {
            "start": 196,
            "end": 200,
            "text": "TG Vow."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Honesty.",
            "prettyString": "TG Honesty",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Honesty",
                "entryId": "tg-honesty",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "TG Vow.",
            "prettyString": "TG Vow",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Vow",
                "entryId": "tg-vow",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:8",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "But behold, here is one thing in which we may have great joy. For behold, in the twenty and sixth year, I, Helaman, did march at the head of these two thousand young men to the city of Judea, to assist Antipus, whom ye had appointed a leader over the people of that part of the land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 147,
            "end": 159,
            "text": "Alma 53:22."
          },
          {
            "start": 185,
            "end": 190,
            "text": "Alma 57:11."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 53:22.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 53:22",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 53,
                    "end": 53,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 22,
                        "end": 22
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "raw": "Alma 57:11.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 57:11",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 57,
                    "end": 57,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 11,
                        "end": 11
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:9",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And I did join my two thousand sons, (for they are worthy to be called sons) to the army of Antipus, in which strength Antipus did rejoice exceedingly; for behold, his army had been reduced by the Lamanites because their forces had slain a vast number of our men, for which cause we have to mourn.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 35,
            "text": "Alma 56:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 56:17.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 56:17",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 56,
                    "end": 56,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 17,
                        "end": 17
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:10",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Nevertheless, we may console ourselves in this point, that they have died in the cause of their country and of their God, yea, and they are happy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 140,
            "end": 145,
            "text": "Alma 28:12."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 28:12.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 28:12",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 28,
                    "end": 28,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 12,
                        "end": 12
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:11",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Lamanites had also retained many prisoners, all of whom are chief captains, for none other have they spared alive. And we suppose that they are now at this time in the land of Nephi; it is so if they are not slain.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 74,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "Alma 52:19."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 52:19.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 52:19",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 52,
                    "end": 52,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 19,
                        "end": 19
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:12",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And now these are the cities of which the Lamanites have obtained possession by the shedding of the blood of so many of our valiant men:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:13",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "The land of Manti, or the city of Manti, and the city of Zeezrom, and the city of Cumeni, and the city of Antiparah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "Alma 43:22."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 88,
            "text": "Alma 57:7 (7–34)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 43:22.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 43:22",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 43,
                    "end": 43,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 22,
                        "end": 22
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:14",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And these are the cities which they possessed when I arrived at the city of Judea; and I found Antipus and his men toiling with their might to fortify the city.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:15",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, and they were depressed in body as well as in spirit, for they had fought valiantly by day and toiled by night to maintain their cities; and thus they had suffered great afflictions of every kind.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:16",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And now they were determined to conquer in this place or die; therefore you may well suppose that this little force which I brought with me, yea, those sons of mine, gave them great hopes and much joy.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 152,
            "end": 156,
            "text": "Alma 56:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 56:10.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 56:10",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 56,
                    "end": 56,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 10,
                        "end": 10
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:17",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And now it came to pass that when the Lamanites saw that Antipus had received a greater strength to his army, they were compelled by the orders of Ammoron to not come against the city of Judea, or against us, to battle.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:18",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus were we favored of the Lord; for had they come upon us in this our weakness they might have perhaps destroyed our little army; but thus were we preserved.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:19",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "They were commanded by Ammoron to maintain those cities which they had taken. And thus ended the twenty and sixth year. And in the commencement of the twenty and seventh year we had prepared our city and ourselves for defence.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:20",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Now we were desirous that the Lamanites should come upon us; for we were not desirous to make an attack upon them in their strongholds.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:21",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that we kept spies out round about, to watch the movements of the Lamanites, that they might not pass us by night nor by day to make an attack upon our other cities which were on the northward.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:22",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "For we knew in those cities they were not sufficiently strong to meet them; therefore we were desirous, if they should pass by us, to fall upon them in their rear, and thus bring them up in the rear at the same time they were met in the front. We supposed that we could overpower them; but behold, we were disappointed in this our desire.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:23",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "They durst not pass by us with their whole army, neither durst they with a part, lest they should not be sufficiently strong and they should fall.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:24",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "Neither durst they march down against the city of Zarahemla; neither durst they cross the head of Sidon, over to the city of Nephihah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:25",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus, with their forces, they were determined to maintain those cities which they had taken.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:26",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "And now it came to pass in the second month of this year, there was brought unto us many provisions from the fathers of those my two thousand sons.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:27",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And also there were sent two thousand men unto us from the land of Zarahemla. And thus we were prepared with ten thousand men, and provisions for them, and also for their wives and their children.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:28",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "And the Lamanites, thus seeing our forces increase daily, and provisions arrive for our support, they began to be fearful, and began to sally forth, if it were possible to put an end to our receiving provisions and strength.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:29",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Now when we saw that the Lamanites began to grow uneasy on this wise, we were desirous to bring a stratagem into effect upon them; therefore Antipus ordered that I should march forth with my little sons to a neighboring city, as if we were carrying provisions to a neighboring city.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 226,
            "end": 228,
            "text": "Alma 52:21; 58:1."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 52:21; 58:1.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 52:21; 58:1",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 52,
                    "end": 52,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 21,
                        "end": 21
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "start": 58,
                    "end": 58,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 1,
                        "end": 1
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:30",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "And we were to march near the city of Antiparah, as if we were going to the city beyond, in the borders by the seashore.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:31",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that we did march forth, as if with our provisions, to go to that city.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:32",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that Antipus did march forth with a part of his army, leaving the remainder to maintain the city. But he did not march forth until I had gone forth with my little army, and came near the city Antiparah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:33",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, in the city Antiparah were stationed the strongest army of the Lamanites; yea, the most numerous.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 34,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:34",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 34
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that when they had been informed by their spies, they came forth with their army and marched against us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 35,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:35",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 35
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that we did flee before them, northward. And thus we did lead away the most powerful army of the Lamanites;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 36,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:36",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 36
      },
      {
        "text": "Yea, even to a considerable distance, insomuch that when they saw the army of Antipus pursuing them, with their might, they did not turn to the right nor to the left, but pursued their march in a straight course after us; and, as we suppose, it was their intent to slay us before Antipus should overtake them, and this that they might not be surrounded by our people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 37,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:37",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 37
      },
      {
        "text": "And now Antipus, beholding our danger, did speed the march of his army. But behold, it was night; therefore they did not overtake us, neither did Antipus overtake them; therefore we did camp for the night.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 38,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:38",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 38
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that before the dawn of the morning, behold, the Lamanites were pursuing us. Now we were not sufficiently strong to contend with them; yea, I would not suffer that my little sons should fall into their hands; therefore we did continue our march, and we took our march into the wilderness.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 39,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:39",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 39
      },
      {
        "text": "Now they durst not turn to the right nor to the left lest they should be surrounded; neither would I turn to the right nor to the left lest they should overtake me, and we could not stand against them, but be slain, and they would make their escape; and thus we did flee all that day into the wilderness, even until it was dark.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 40,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:40",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 40
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that again, when the light of the morning came we saw the Lamanites upon us, and we did flee before them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 41,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:41",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 41
      },
      {
        "text": "But it came to pass that they did not pursue us far before they halted; and it was in the morning of the third day of the seventh month.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 42,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:42",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 42
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, whether they were overtaken by Antipus we knew not, but I said unto my men: Behold, we know not but they have halted for the purpose that we should come against them, that they might catch us in their snare;",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 43,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:43",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 43
      },
      {
        "text": "Therefore what say ye, my sons, will ye go against them to battle?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 44,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Alma 56:44",
        "book": "Alma",
        "chapter": 56,
        "verse": 44
      },
      {
        "text": "And now I say unto you, my beloved brother Moroni, that never had I seen so great courage, nay, not amongst all the Nephites.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 81,
            "text": "Alma 19:10."
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Courage."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 45,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Alma 19:10.",
            "prettyString": "Alma 19:10",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "alma",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 19,
                    "end": 19,
                    "verses": [
                      {
